                <pb facs="0254" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg120"/>

                <head>No. 90.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Hall.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 28,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 543.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 763, of the 6th
                    instant, relative to the Italian claim against Salvador 5 also your telegram of
                    the 25th instant.</p>
                <p>I desire to express the satisfaction with which the Department learns that this
                    question has reached an amicable adjustment, and to add that the result is
                    particularly gratifying in view of the manner in which it was obtained.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your full report of the nature and extent of your good offices in
                    bringing the parties into mutual accord,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
